  "text": "The largest bone in the human body is the femur, also known as the thigh bone.\n\n***\n\nA cavern vast, of knowledge deep,\nWhere human curiosity sleeps\nIn silent halls, in rows of bound,\nEach spine a world, each page profound.\n\nA portal wide to lives unknown,\nTo seeds of thought and truths sown.\nThe wise old keeper, gray and stern,\nKnows every story, every turn.\n\nHe watches o’er the endless shelf,\nWhere wisdom waits for those who delve,\nIn every book, a life unfolds,\nA story of the human souls."
